@startuml sdd-05_dev_mode_state
title SDD-05 — dev.mode (UML **state machine diagram**)\nRead once at boot; the Welcome switch writes user_config.json and the next run applies it (ADR D14).
[*] --> Booting
Booting --> UserMode : dev.mode == false\n(app_config default, user_config, or no --dev)
Booting --> DevMode : dev.mode == true\n(--dev wins for this run, else user_config)

state UserMode {
  [*] --> Welcome_U
  Welcome_U : Start → trading
  Welcome_U : switch "Developer mode" OFF → ON
  Welcome_U --> RestartPending_U : toggle writes user_config.json\n(dev.mode = true)
  RestartPending_U : banner "takes effect after restart"
  RestartPending_U : [Restart now] → QProcess.startDetached(argv); quit
}

state DevMode {
  [*] --> Welcome_D
  Welcome_D : Start → trading
  Welcome_D : Dev Board visible in sidebar; probes registered
  Welcome_D --> RestartPending_D : toggle writes user_config.json\n(dev.mode = false)
}

RestartPending_U --> [*] : quit; new process boots → DevMode
RestartPending_D --> [*] : quit; new process boots → UserMode
note bottom of DevMode
  No hot reload: modules and surfaces are
  registered only at boot (ADR D14, "out of scope: hot reload").
end note
@enduml
